      "y": 1248,
      "w": 448,
      "h": 224,
      "label": "Notes",
      "props": {
        "text": "Run mode models feed loads (Redis first, misses read the posts store), image fetches (ending at the CDN) and likes/comments (written to the engagement store, counted asynchronously). Photo bytes go phone to object storage with a presigned URL; the object-created event drives resizing, and the post is created only once its variants exist. Fan-out writes timelines into Redis only for followers active in the last 30 days and never for accounts above 1M followers, whose posts are merged at read time. Sized for the 2x peak with one zone lost: 225 API instances."
      }
